<html lang="en"><head><meta charset="UTF-8"/><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"/><title>Work — Sam Connelly</title></head><body><div class="shell"><header class="top"><a class="brand" href="/">Sam Connelly</a><nav class="nav" aria-label="Main navigation"><a href="/">Home</a><a href="/work">Work</a><a href="/reading">Reading</a><a href="/notes">Notes</a></nav></header><main><section class="page-heading"><div class="eyebrow">Experience & projects</div><h1>Work</h1><p>I'm interested in the intersection of business questions, technical systems, and practical execution.</p></section><section class="section prose"><h2>Experience</h2><p>Over 7 years in marketing technology consulting, working across customer data platforms, analytics, technical architecture, and growth systems. My work spans discovery, solution design, implementation, and helping teams put new capabilities to use.</p><p>I've worked on 25+ CDP deployments, often helping teams connect technical implementation decisions back to the problems they're trying to solve.</p><p class="muted">A detailed resume and career timeline will be added here.</p></section><section class="section prose" id="coaching"><h2><a href="/projects/ai-coaching-staff">AI Coaching Staff ↗</a> <span class="tag">In progress</span></h2><p>A personal project exploring whether AI can turn actual work into useful coaching. The system reviews work artifacts, identifies strengths and opportunities, and connects feedback to deliberate practice over time.</p><p>It's a private, laptop-first project. I'll share product thinking, architecture, and sanitized examples here as it develops—not client material or personal coaching data.</p></section></main><footer class="footer"><span>© {new Date().getFullYear()} Sam Connelly</span><a href="/">Back home ↑</a></footer></div></body></html>
